    "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\nInstall `nvidia-cudnn-frontend[cutedsl]==1.31.0` in the dev environment, upgrading from 1.29.0. Regenerate `uv.lock` with uv 0.7.2 in the Megatron-LM CI container. Only cuDNN Frontend changes version; existing transitive dependencies and compatible build/Transformer Engine lower bounds are preserved.\n\nUpstream release: https://github.com/NVIDIA/cudnn-frontend/releases/tag/v1.31.0\n\n## Validation\n\n- `uv lock --check` passed in the CI container with `TMS_CUDA_MAJOR=13`.\n- Installation passed in an isolated environment on the pinned `nvcr.io/nvidia/pytorch:26.09-py3` base, using dependency constraints from `uv.lock`.\n- Verified Frontend version 1.31.0; `cudnn`, `cudnn.DSA`, and `cutlass.cute` imports passed. Loaded cuDNN backend version: 92600.\n- `git diff --check` passed; all 12 locked wheel records match published PyPI metadata.\n- GPU execution and numerical tests were not run locally: the host reports an NVML driver/library version mismatch. GPU validation remains pending CI.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
